<%- include('partials/head') %>

<section class="hiw-hero">
  <p class="hiw-step-label">How it works</p>
  <h1>A public side to learn and trade help.<br>A private side to do the work.</h1>
  <p class="lead">NoBossly is free. Everyone gets the public community and a dashboard built for their kind of business. Members of accelerator programs also get private cohorts that nobody outside can see.</p>
  <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:center;margin-top:1.5rem">
    <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/signup">Join free &rarr;</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href="/paths">See the paths</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row single" style="margin-top:2rem">
  <div>
    <p class="hiw-step-label">Step 1</p>
    <h2>&#x1F9ED; Pick your path</h2>
    <p class="muted">Creator, freelancer, coach or consultant, local service, shop or café, online store, physical product, apps and software, or still figuring it out. Then answer three or four questions about where you are. It takes about a minute, you can skip it, and you can change any of it later.</p>
    <p class="muted">Your path decides what your dashboard puts first. It never locks anything away: every tool is open to everyone.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row">
  <div>
    <p class="hiw-step-label">Step 2</p>
    <h2>&#x1F4CA; Work from your dashboard</h2>
    <p class="muted">Your dashboard shows where you are and the next real step to take, plus:</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li><strong>Your number</strong>: the one that tells you it's working for your path, logged each week or month with the trend beside it</li>
      <li><strong>Boards</strong> for the work in motion: clients, jobs, content, deals, suppliers, an opening plan. Anything with a date lands on one calendar</li>
      <li><strong>Checklists</strong> for the must-dos: licences, contracts, launch steps, renewals with reminder dates</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="card" style="align-self:center;padding:1.5rem">
    <span class="tag">A freelancer's dashboard</span>
    <p style="margin:.7rem 0 .2rem"><strong>Where you are:</strong> some regular clients</p>
    <p class="muted small" style="margin:0 0 .7rem">Next: collect five testimonials and raise your rate for new clients.</p>
    <p style="margin:0"><strong>Billable income:</strong> $2,400 <span class="muted small">▲ $600 on last month</span></p>
    <p class="muted small" style="margin:.5rem 0 0">Client pipeline · Invoices · Contract essentials · Getting paid</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row single">
  <div>
    <p class="hiw-step-label">Step 3</p>
    <h2>&#x1F9F0; Plan it in your workspace</h2>
    <p class="muted">The worksheets an accelerator would hand you, private to you:</p>
    <div class="grid" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <div class="card"><h4>Shape the idea</h4><p class="muted small">Idea refiner, Lean Canvas, Business Model Canvas, customer persona, and an options matrix for choosing between ideas.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h4>Make the case</h4><p class="muted small">Business plan, elevator pitch with every version kept, and an offer or proposal builder.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h4>Run the numbers</h4><p class="muted small">Pricing &amp; margin, break-even, start-up budget, unit cost, tax set-aside, quit date, and a budgeter with an income log.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h4>Ask the market</h4><p class="muted small">A survey maker with a public link and no account needed to answer, plus a customer-interview log.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h4>Keep moving</h4><p class="muted small">Tasks, goals, and a milestone tracker in your own words.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row">
  <div>
    <p class="hiw-step-label">Step 4</p>
    <h2>&#x1F4AC; Use the public side</h2>
    <p class="muted">Everyone who signs up can use it, and everyone there is fitting this around something else.</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li><strong>Feed and Q&amp;A</strong>: ask, answer, and share what you're working on</li>
      <li><strong>Help &amp; exchange</strong>: ask for help, offer yours, or swap skills. Say thanks when it's done</li>
      <li><strong>Get feedback</strong> on your idea, pitch or pricing from other members</li>
      <li><strong>Groups</strong>: public, private, or invite-only, each with a Monday and Friday check-in thread</li>
      <li><strong>Collaborators</strong>: find a partner or the skill you're missing</li>
      <li><strong>Challenges and public cohorts</strong>, then share your results</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted small">Contact details stay out of public posts. People connect through NoBossly messages.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card" style="padding:1.5rem;align-self:center">
    <span class="tag">Help &amp; exchange</span>
    <p style="margin:.7rem 0 .2rem"><strong>Ask:</strong> Can someone look over my pricing page?</p>
    <p class="muted small" style="margin:0 0 .7rem">Marketing &amp; SEO · free</p>
    <p class="muted small" style="margin:0">2 members offered to help. Pick one, and say thanks when it's done.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row single">
  <div>
    <p class="hiw-step-label">Step 5 · If you're in a program</p>
    <h2>&#x1F512; Work through it in a private cohort</h2>
    <p class="muted">Accelerators and programs run their cohorts on NoBossly. A cohort is invite-only, and nothing in it is visible outside: not the posts, not the members, not the work.</p>
    <div class="grid" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <div class="card"><h4>For members</h4><p class="muted small">Join with your program's invite link. See assignments with due dates, hand in a copy of your canvas, plan or board, get feedback, and resubmit. Your workspace stays private.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h4>For program teams</h4><p class="muted small">Create cohorts, invite your participants, set assignments from any worksheet or board, and review what comes in. The activity view shows who's moving and who's gone quiet, with a CSV for reports. It shows counts and dates, never what anyone wrote.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta-band">
  <h2>Free. No card, no catch.</h2>
  <p class="muted">Every path, every tool, the community, groups and cohorts are free.</p>
  <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" style="margin-top:1.1rem;display:inline-block" href="/signup">Join free &rarr;</a>
</section>

<style>
.hiw-hero { text-align: center; padding: 2.5rem 1rem 1.5rem; }
.hiw-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.6rem); max-width: 760px; margin: .5rem auto .75rem; }
.hiw-hero .lead { max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; }
.hiw-step-label { font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--green, #1b5e38); margin: 0 0 .35rem; }
</style>

<%- include('partials/foot') %>
